<section class="section has-text-left">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="has-text-weight-bold is-size-1 is-size-3-mobile is-uppercase">Taco Bell + Cheez-It</p>
    <p class="projectdescription is-size-5">
      For the Cheez-It Crunchwrap Supreme launch, Taco Bell set out to create more than a product reveal. As Design Director, I oversaw a playful, tech-forward brand expression and carried it through the design of the space, ensuring the night felt like a cultural moment worth sharing.

Guests entered through a colossal Crunchwrap tunnel into an environment pulsing with neon and sly tech details. Cat robots delivered Crunchwrap bites, a hologram machine transformed influencers into larger-than-life Crunchwraps, and custom cocktails kept the energy high. Every touchpoint was designed to surprise guests and spark content.
<br><br>
The result was an experience that turned a menu launch into a night of culture, energy, and shareable moments, proof Taco Bell could merge food and futurism in a way only they could.
    <p class="has-text-weight-bold is-size-4">Collaborators:</p>
    <p class="collabnames is-family-secondary has-text-weight-bold is-size-4 is-italic"> Alexander Turk // Keirstin Fernandes // Matt Pamer <br> Nath Mallon // Anthony Baxter</p>
  </div>
</section>

